<title>USA: Illinois direct hogs up $1.00-1.50 - USDA.</title>
<headline>Illinois direct hogs up $1.00-1.50 - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>SPRINGFIELD 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA said barrows and gilts were $1.00 to $1.50 higher. Demand was good. Top $50.00 per cwt.</p>
<p>US 1-2 230-260 lbs. 48.50-50.00, few early 47.50-48.50</p>
<p>Sows - unevenly up $0.50-1.50. Top $49.00.</p>
<p>    US 1-3    300-400 lbs. 40.00-43.50</p>
<p>		  400-500 lbs. 41.00-45.50</p>
<p>		  500-600 lbs. 46.00-49.00</p>
</text>
